## Context

19 data portals (SEN 8, ZAF 8, IDN 2, VNM 1). Their snapshots are mostly HTML,
with a few JSON, JavaScript and octet-stream objects (content types measured
over the 115: 66 HTML, 38 PDF, 6 octet-stream, 2 xlsx, 2 JSON, 2 JavaScript).
A dashboard's HTML shell may hold no data at all; what the stored bytes contain
is not known yet.

## Work

- First, inspect each of the 19 snapshots and record what it holds: data, a
  shell around an API, or nothing extractable. That inspection is the
  deliverable that decides scope; a portal whose bytes hold no data gets a
  recorded disposition and, if its API matters, a follow-up acquisition
  ticket (acquisition is out of scope here).
- For those that hold data: an ingestion script writes the lines, with a
  manifest naming the snapshot, the row count and the field spec (storage
  contract § 3). A bulk line is adjudicated only when an observation cites it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All 19 portals have a recorded content verdict (data, shell, nothing)
- [ ] Each portal with data has lines and a manifest; the PR reviews the manifest
- [ ] Lines of previously extracted documents are byte-identical
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
